Achmage Workbench — rhwp v0.9.0 engine patch of Workbench's own (third_party/hop/patches-0.9.0).
Origin: Workbench 0023 (0.9.0-workbench.4) — the H4b review M1 rule of 0.9.0-workbench.3's own port of Ieum 0020, carried onto IeumOffice's 0020/0034 forms
Status: ported
What it changes: Ieum's `topbottom_float_anchor_flow_bottom` (typeset.rs, Ieum 0020; used by section/flow.rs and by `first_stale_topbottom_float_anchor`) moves ANY anchor paragraph that starts inside its paper/page top-and-bottom object below it. Workbench's own 0020 port (0.9.0-workbench.2/.3) had limited this to anchors without visible text after the H4b review (M1): samples/issue5941 roadmap, an 11-line paragraph with text anchoring a page-high frame on page 158. With Ieum's form the roadmap still has 302 pages, but page 158 draws 31 text lines instead of Hancom's 36 (35 body + 1 note) and page 159's body text starts at the top of the body, over the picture group drawn at 140–454 px (0.9.0-workbench.3: below it, from 525 px). This restores the rule: an anchor with visible text (not white space, not a control, not U+FFFC) keeps its stored lines.
Regression test: apps/host/src/hwp-anchor-space.test.ts (Ieum's fixture with the anchor text varied: empty and space-only anchors below the box, a text anchor keeps its band line — failed on Ieum's form: 18 vs 17 lines on page 2); the roadmap probe (302 pages, page 158 36 lines) in the unit report (the sample is not in this repository).

